{"id":170475,"accession_number":"2012.72.1","share_license_status":"CC0","tombstone":"Spring and Autumn Farming (Spring), 1700s. Kō Sūkoku (Japanese, 1730–1804). Six-panel folding screen, ink, light color, gold, and silver on paper; overall: 170.2 x 353.5 cm (67 x 139 3/16 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift of Dr. Norman Zaworski, 2012.72.1","current_location":null,"title":"Spring and Autumn Farming (Spring)","creation_date":"1700s","creation_date_earliest":1750,"creation_date_latest":1799,"artists_tags":["male"],"culture":["Japan, Edo period (1615–1868)"],"technique":"Six-panel folding screen, ink, light color, gold, and silver on paper","support_materials":[],"department":"Japanese Art","collection":"ASIAN - Folding screen","type":"Painting","measurements":"Overall: 170.2 x 353.5 cm (67 x 139 3/16 in.)","dimensions":{"overall":{"height":1.702,"height_inch":67,"height_inch_fraction":0,"width":3.535,"width_inch":139,"width_inch_fraction":0.1875}},"state_of_the_work":null,"edition_of_the_work":null,"copyright":null,"inscriptions":[{"inscription":"Signature of the artist: \"Enrin san jin Rakushisai ko Sukoku ga\" (each screen)","inscription_translation":null,"inscription_remark":null,"sortorder":null}],"exhibitions":{"current":[{"id":300223,"title":"Japanese Gallery 235 Rotation","description":"<i>Japanese Gallery 235 Rotation</i>. The Cleveland Museum of Art (organizer) (January 2-July 9, 2018).","opening_date":"2018-01-02T05:00:00"}],"legacy":[{"description":"<em>Japanese Screens</em>. The Cleveland Museum of Art, Cleveland, OH (1977).","opening_date":"1977-01-01T00:00:00"}]},"provenance":[{"description":"Dr. Norman Zaworski [1920–2013], Cleveland, OH, given to the Cleveland Museum of Art","citations":[],"footnotes":null,"date":"?–2012","sortorder":1},{"description":"The Cleveland Museum of Art, Cleveland, OH","citations":[],"footnotes":[],"date":"2012–","sortorder":2}],"find_spot":null,"related_works":[],"former_accession_numbers":[],"did_you_know":null,"early_education_description":null,"artlens_description":null,"description":"These screens present the cycle of the farming year, starting with spring at right and ending with fall at left. Close examination of these screens reveals moments of games and amusement, the enjoyment of meals as well as intellectual and spiritual pursuits interspersed among the scenes of cultivating and preparing the rice harvest.<br><br>The artist Kō Sūkoku is considered the 18th-century heir in style and attitude to Hanabusa Itchō (1652–1724). Itchō’s work incorporated elements from Kano school, ukiyo-e, and literati styles of painting. Kō trained with one of Hanabusa’s pupils, Sawaki Sūshi, who was best known for scenes depicting everyday life and customs.","external_resources":{"wikidata":["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q60480993"],"internet_archive":["https://archive.org/details/clevelandart-2012.72.1-spring-and-autumn-fa"]},"citations":[{"citation":"\"New in the Galleries.” <em>Cleveland Art: Cleveland Museum of Art Members Magazine</em> 58. no. 1 (January/February 2018): Back cover.","page_number":"Reproduced and Mentioned: Back cover","url":"https://archive.org/details/CMAMM2018-01/page/n13/mode/2up"}],"url":"https://clevelandart.org/art/2012.72.1","images":{"annotation":null,"web":{"url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/2012.72.1/2012.72.1_web.jpg","width":"1263","height":"572","filesize":"148005","filename":"2012.72.1_web.jpg"},"print":{"url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/2012.72.1/2012.72.1_print.jpg","width":"3400","height":"1540","filesize":"1073649","filename":"2012.72.1_print.jpg"},"full":{"url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/2012.72.1/2012.72.1_full.tif","width":"17044","height":"7724","filesize":"394979944","filename":"2012.72.1_full.tif"}},"alternate_images":[{"web":{"url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/2012.72.1/2012.72.1_alt0_web.jpg","width":"670","height":"893","filesize":"126636"},"print":{"url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.o